Firmament doesn't ship any model. The web app drives a ComfyUI on your PC; the desktop app (cpp\) downloads the
models from its Models tab. Both run these (downloaded separately):
- Krea 2 Turbo (krea2_turbo_bf16-Q4_0.gguf), its text encoder (qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled) and the Wan 2.1 VAE:
  Krea 2 Community License Agreement, https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2
- Krea-2 360 ERP LoRA (krea2_t2i_360_erp_lora_v1.safetensors) by mickmumpitz, under the Krea 2 Community License:
  https://huggingface.co/mickmumpitz/Krea2-360-ERP-LoRAs. Firmament uses its prompt template.
- 4x-UltraSharp V2 Lite (upscaling in the web app), by Kim2091.
- Real-ESRGAN x4plus and x4plus anime 6B (upscaling in the desktop app), Xintao Wang et al., BSD-3-Clause:
  https://github.com/xinntao/Real-ESRGAN

The desktop app (cpp\) ships:
- stable-diffusion.cpp (stable-diffusion.dll) - leejet and contributors - https://github.com/leejet/stable-diffusion.cpp
  - MIT License; with ggml (MIT, https://github.com/ggml-org/ggml)
- NVIDIA CUDA runtime libraries (cudart64_12.dll, cublas64_12.dll, cublasLt64_12.dll), redistributed under the
  NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit End User License Agreement - https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/eula/
- Microsoft Visual C++ runtime and OpenMP DLLs, redistributable under the Visual Studio licence
- SDL2 (zlib), Dear ImGui (MIT), stb_image / stb_image_write (MIT / public domain)

Python packages: Flask and Waitress (BSD-3-Clause), NumPy (BSD-3-Clause), Pillow (MIT-CMU),
websocket-client (Apache-2.0), segno (BSD-3-Clause).
